-
-`Esc` cancels a command line.
+| Command          | Action                              |
+|------------------|-------------------------------------|
+| `:w`             | save current buffer                 |
+| `:e <file>`      | open a file in a buffer             |
+| `:e` / `:new`    | new empty buffer                    |
+| `:bn` / `:bp`    | next / previous buffer              |
+| `:ls`            | list buffers (`%` = current)        |
+| `:bd` / `:bd!`   | close buffer (`!` forces, discarding changes) |
+| `:q`             | close buffer; quit when it's the last |
+| `:q!`            | close without saving / quit         |
+| `:wq` / `:x`     | save and close / quit               |
+
+`Esc` cancels a command line. Opening a file that is already open switches to
+it instead of duplicating it. The status line shows `current/total` buffers
+and marks the current one with `*` when modified. Each buffer keeps its own
+cursor position and undo history.
 
